# Source is text, even when a stray byte says otherwise.
#
# Git decides text-or-binary by looking for a NUL in the first few KB. One
# such byte — a typo, a bad paste — and the file stops having diffs: reviews
# show "Binary file not shown", `git grep` answers without a line, and two
# branches touching it can only conflict whole, since there is no three-way
# merge for a binary. `use-dev-warnings.ts` spent two months that way.
#
# `diff` alone, not `text`: this settles how git *shows* these files and
# nothing else. `text` would also turn on end-of-line normalisation, which
# would rewrite working copies that have nothing wrong with them.
*.ts    diff
*.tsx   diff
*.mjs   diff
*.css   diff
*.json  diff
*.md    diff
*.yml   diff
